    "module_designation": "Not applicable",
    "description": "Class III, mains or battery-operated, self-indicating, single-interval, non-automatic weighing instrument, designated the AWB120. Not designed for direct sales to the public. Main features: pole-mounted LCD display with function keys and LED indicators (low battery, checkweighing); indicator plastic enclosure; aluminium die-casting load receptor (420 x 520 mm) with stainless steel pan; level indicator (at the base of the pole) and adjustable feet. Devices: initial zero setting device, semi-automatic zero setting device, zero tracking device, zero indicator, net indicator, determination of stable equilibrium, stable equilibrium indicator, semi-automatic subtractive tare balancing device, checking of display, weight accumulation, printing, checkweighing, coarse filter mode to allow weighing of unstable samples. Interface: RS232. Sealing: weighing platform bears the serial number of the rating plate located on the indicator, secured by sealing or destructible form; calibration mode is password-protected with non-editable counters CALxxx and OPTxxx displayed at power-up and written on a tamper-evident label."
